          %h1#introduction Introduction
          %p
            This entry is about the work by David Ben-Zvi, John Francis and David Nadler on application of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categorical
            realization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+function+theory"} geometric function theory
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} extended quantum field theory
            in the context in which Jacob Lurie proved the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+tangle+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
          %p So far this work is presented in the two articles
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %strong IntTrans
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ben-Zvi"} David Ben-Zvi
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"} John Francis
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Nadler"} David Nadler
                %em Integral transforms and Drinfeld Centers in Derived Geometry
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0805.0157"}> arXiv
                )
              %p
                appendix:
                %em Morita equivalence for convolution categories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://pages.uoregon.edu/njp/bfn.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %strong CharTheo
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ben-Zvi"} David Ben-Zvi
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Nadler"} David Nadler
                %em The Character Theory of a Complex Group
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0904.1247"}> arXiv
                )
          .query
            %p
              This entry is supposed to be the
              = succeed "Lab-working" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-function" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "-Caf\u00E9" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2009/04/journal_club_geometric_infinit.html"} Journal Club – Geometric ∞-Function Theory
            %p The idea is to
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  jointly discuss at the
                  = succeed "Caf\u00E9" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %li
                %p add here, step by step, links to keywords appearing in these sections, and create the corresponding entries describing them.
              %li
                %p This is supposed to be a recursive and iterative process, which, if successful, will eventually create here a useful repository of entries that describe and explain the various aspects of the topic.
          %h1#basic_idea_in_three_words Basic idea in three words
          %p
            Geometric
            = succeed "-function" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-categorification"} ∞-categorification
            of the following basic fact of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+calculus"} matrix calculus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
