          %p
            That’s it, essentially. The point is that this simple statement then turns out to be a powerful organization and unification tool for lots of structures appearing in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} functorial quantum field theory
          %h1#timeline Timeline
          %p We will try to proceed as follows: we go through the sections of the two articles, step by step, possibly several steps for one section. Each week on Monday, one of us produces a “report” on the section he or she was assigned to read.
          %p This “report” would try to give a rough idea of what is going on in a given section. A report may be anything from a heap of questions (likely) to a complete detailed rederivation of all the details (maybe not quite as likely, but let’s not exclude it!) The more questions, the more we all get involved, which is the whole point of doing this online.
          %p
            I (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs
            ) am imagining that whatever the report is like, it consists of
